Licences of the components in wine.app

Each component, its licence, where its licence texts are in this bundle, and where its source is. SOURCE (beside this
file) names the exact inputs this bundle was built from: the commits of our forks (https://github.com/Mac-Neutron:
upstream with MacNeutron's changes; each tree's *_SERIES is its pin, "dev" for a tree built with unpublished work),
the other upstream commits, and the source tarballs' URLs and SHA-256. The pins are in the MacNeutron repository
(https://github.com/Mac-Neutron/MacNeutron), at the commit SOURCE's MACNEUTRON_COMMIT names. NOTICES.md quotes the notices that live only in source headers. Not legal advice.

Wine 11.20 (the loader, wineserver, Wine's libraries and programs)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Texts: wine/LICENSE, wine/COPYING.LIB, wine/AUTHORS; Wine's vendored libraries are
  listed in wine/NOTICES.md, and GSM (wine/gsm-COPYRIGHT) and FAudio (zlib licence, wine/faudio-LICENSE) carry their
  own texts. msync (from CrossOver) and its helpers adapted from Apple's xnu (APSL-2.0): NOTICES.md. libxess.dll's XeSS
  declarations, copied from Intel's public headers (MIT): NOTICES.md.
  The ARM64 string routines in msvcrt.dll, ucrtbase.dll and msvcr80-120.dll come from Arm Optimized Routines (MIT): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://github.com/Mac-Neutron/wine.git at WINE_COMMIT (pinned in wine-arm64/pins): Wine
  (https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine.git) with MacNeutron's changes.

FEX (libarm64ecfex.dll and libarm64ecfex.so: runs x86_64 code)
  Licence: MIT, fex/LICENSE; MacNeutron's changes to it are MIT too. Compiled-in externals, each with its text in
  fex/: fmt (MIT), xxhash (BSD-2-Clause), tiny-json (MIT), unordered_dense (MIT), rpmalloc (0BSD), cephes (BSD),
  range-v3 (Boost Software Licence 1.0), cpp-optparse (MIT). SoftFloat-3e (BSD-3-Clause), the VIXL utilities
  (BSD-3-Clause), musl and Arm's routines (MIT), Madeira's commits (MIT grant) and eac-arm64-emulation-poc's (MIT): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://github.com/Mac-Neutron/FEX.git at FEX_COMMIT (pinned in wine-arm64/pins): FEX
  (https://github.com/FEX-Emu/FEX.git) with MacNeutron's changes, its submodules at the FEX_SUBMODULE_* commits.

DXMT (the Direct3D to Metal DLLs in ../DXMT/aarch64-windows, winemetal.dll and winemetal.so)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Texts: ../DXMT/LICENSE, ../DXMT/COPYING.LIB, ../DXMT/LICENSE.OLD (MIT, for releases up
  to v0.80). DXBCParser (MIT, Microsoft) and the constexpr GUID parser (MIT): NOTICES.md. nvngx.dll, nvapi64.dll,
  dxgi.dll, d3d10core.dll, winemetal.dll and winemetal.so are Rust and link Rust's standard library:
  mtld3d/rust/COPYRIGHT-library.html and the texts it names in mtld3d/rust/licenses (mtld3d's copy, from the same
  toolchain). winemetal.so also links objc2, its framework crates, block2, dispatch2, libc and bitflags: mtld3d/crates,
  listed in mtld3d/crates/INDEX.
  Source: https://github.com/Mac-Neutron/DXMTRS.git at DXMT_COMMIT (pinned in dxmt/pins; ../DXMT/version names it too):
  DXMT (https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt.git) with MacNeutron's changes, its submodules at the DXMT_SUBMODULE_* commits.

mtld3d 0.14.1 (Direct3D 9: d3d9.dll and mtld3d.dll in lib/wine/aarch64-windows, mtld3d.so in lib/wine/aarch64-unix)
  Licence: zlib, mtld3d/LICENSE. The crates its binaries link (snmalloc-sys among them, MIT, with MacNeutron's ARM64EC
  change): mtld3d/crates, each crate's own licence files, and mtld3d/crates/INDEX naming every crate and its terms;
  snmalloc's C++, which snmalloc-sys compiles in, MIT, Microsoft Corporation, mtld3d/crates/snmalloc-sys-*/
  LICENSE-snmalloc. Rust's standard library, which the binaries link: mtld3d/rust/COPYRIGHT-library.html and the texts
  it names in mtld3d/rust/licenses, from the Rust toolchain dxmt/pins names (MTLD3D_RUST). In the game VM, the x86-64
  and i386 d3d9.dll and mtld3d.dll also link DXMT's rust_pe_rt.c (LGPL-2.1-or-later, ../DXMT/LICENSE); the Mac's don't.
  Source: DXMTRS's src/d3d9 (https://github.com/Mac-Neutron/DXMTRS.git at DXMT_COMMIT, snmalloc-sys in its
  vendor/snmalloc-sys), altered from https://github.com/athei/mtld3d.git release 0.14.1 (0c172127); the crates from
  crates.io at the versions DXMTRS's Cargo.lock pins.

LLVM 15.0.7 (linked statically into winemetal.so)
  Licence: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, llvm/LICENSE.TXT; its regular-expression code, llvm/COPYRIGHT.regex;
  ConvertUTF (Unicode, Inc.) and the regex notice: NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project.git at LLVM_TAG (llvmorg-15.0.7), unmodified.

llvm-mingw, development head (the Windows-side toolchain: DXMT's DLLs, winemetal.dll and libarm64ecfex.dll link its
runtime)
  Licence: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, llvm-mingw/LICENSE.TXT; the mingw-w64 runtime,
  llvm-mingw/COPYING.MinGW-w64-runtime.txt.
  Source: MacNeutron's own build (the repository's dxmt/llvm-mingw.sh) of https://github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw.git at
  dxmt/pins' LLVM_MINGW_COMMIT, with LLVM from https://github.com/Mac-Neutron/llvm-project.git at dxmt/pins'
  LLVM_MINGW_LLVM (LLVM with MacNeutron's changes); the mingw-w64 sources its scripts fetch are listed at https://github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw.

FreeType 2.15.0, development head (libfreetype.6.dylib: text rendering in win32u and dwrite)
  Licence: the FreeType License (FTL), elected from FreeType's FTL-or-GPL-2.0 choice. Texts: freetype/LICENSE.TXT,
  freetype/FTL.TXT. Built without PNG, HarfBuzz or Brotli; it links the system's zlib and bzip2. The BDF and PCF
  drivers (X11-style licence): freetype/bdf-README, freetype/pcf-README; its hashing code (MIT-style): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype.git at FREETYPE_COMMIT, with its dlg submodule, unmodified,
  pinned in the repository's wine-arm64/deps.pins and bootstrapped and built by wine-arm64/build.sh.

gnutls 3.8.13-153-g0e7b36b5, development head (libgnutls.30.dylib: TLS for secur32's schannel, PFX import and export
for crypt32)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, gnutls/COPYING.LESSERv2. The libunistring it includes is LGPL-3.0-or-later:
  gnutls/COPYING.LESSERv3 and gnutls/COPYINGv3 (the GPL-3.0 text the LGPL-3.0 builds on). The aarch64 CRYPTOGAMS
  routines (BSD-3-Clause), gnutls/cryptogams-license.txt; inih (BSD-3-Clause), gnutls/inih-LICENSE.txt; randomart
  (BSD-2-Clause, OpenBSD): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://gitlab.com/gnutls/gnutls.git at GNUTLS_COMMIT, with the gnulib its bootstrap copies in, unmodified,
  pinned and built as FreeType is, with libtasn1, nettle and GMP linked in statically.

libtasn1 4.21.0-10-g2b20, development head (linked statically into libgnutls.30.dylib)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, libtasn1/COPYING.LESSERv2.
  Source: https://gitlab.com/gnutls/libtasn1.git at LIBTASN1_COMMIT, unmodified, pinned and built as FreeType is.

nettle 4.0, development head (linked statically into libgnutls.30.dylib)
  Licence: LGPL-3.0-or-later, elected from nettle's LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later choice. Texts:
  nettle/COPYING.LESSERv3, nettle/COPYINGv3.
  Source: https://git.lysator.liu.se/nettle/nettle.git at NETTLE_COMMIT, unmodified, pinned and built as FreeType is.

GMP 6.3.0, development trunk (gmp-next) snapshot 20260920180220 (linked statically into libgnutls.30.dylib)
  Licence: LGPL-3.0-or-later, elected from GMP's LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later choice. Texts:
  gmp/COPYING.LESSERv3, gmp/COPYINGv3.
  Source: https://gmplib.org/download/snapshot/gmp-next/gmp-6.3.0-20260920180220.tar.zst (SHA-256 GMP_SHA256),
  unmodified, pinned and built as FreeType is.

FFmpeg 8.0.git, development head (libavutil.61.dylib, libavcodec.63.dylib, libavformat.63.dylib, libswscale.10.dylib,
libswresample.7.dylib: winedmo's demuxers, and the audio and video decoders macOS doesn't provide)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1; ffmpeg/LICENSE.md names the files under other terms. Built with
  no GPL or nonfree part and without FFmpeg's own H.264, HEVC and AAC decoders. Its notice, the Independent JPEG
  Group's for libavcodec's DCTs, and those of faandct.c (ISC) and avsscanf.c (MIT): NOTICES.md. To use a modified
  FFmpeg, build it and put its dylibs in place of these (lib/wine/aarch64-unix), then sign each of them again: an ad
  hoc signature is enough (codesign -f -s - <dylib>). Leave the loader's signature (Contents/MacOS/wine) as it is: it
  loads libraries signed by anyone, and re-signing it, even ad hoc, drops the entitlement it needs to start.
  Source: https://git.ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg.git at FFMPEG_COMMIT, unmodified, pinned and built as FreeType is, with the
  configure options in the repository's wine-arm64/build.sh.

lsteamclient (lsteamclient.dll and lsteamclient.so: the Steam bridge, from Windows games' Steam API to Mac Steam's
steamclient.dylib)
  Licence: Valve's Steamworks SDK licence, lsteamclient/LICENSE (lsteamclient is Steamworks-SDK-derived); its cxx.h is
  LGPL-2.1-or-later (CodeWeavers, from Wine), lsteamclient/NOTE. It ships by the maintainer's decision of 2026-10-04
  under Valve's Steamworks SDK licence (lsteamclient/).
  Source: https://github.com/Mac-Neutron/Proton.git, its lsteamclient/ folder at LSTEAMCLIENT_COMMIT (pinned in
  wine-arm64/deps.pins): Proton (https://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton.git) with dappermint/winecx's three Mac
  fixes.

MacNeutron (libmacneutron-present.dylib and libmacneutron-present.metallib, the MetalFX presenter)
  Licence: MIT, macneutron/LICENSE; its CMAA2 anti-aliasing shader (libmacneutron-present.metallib) is Apache-2.0
  (Intel), macneutron/CMAA2-LICENSE.txt and NOTICES.md.
  Source: the repository at MACNEUTRON_COMMIT: presenter/present.m and presenter/cmaa2.metal. MacNeutron's changes in
  our forks keep the licence of the tree they change (Wine and DXMT: LGPL-2.1-or-later; FEX: MIT; lsteamclient:
  Valve's terms).

